                 OXXI File Conversion Utility for MaxiPlan
                          by James H. H. Lampert

    This is a very simple utility program, written in AmigaBASIC, for
converting database TEXT files from one format to another.  In order to
use the program, you must supply it with the AmigaBASIC interpreter
that came with your computer.
    When File Converter is run, there is a slight delay, while the menus
and windows are set up.  A welcome message appears, giving summary
instructions.  At this point, the program is entirely under menu control.
The "File" menu has the options "Perform Conversion" (self explanatory),
"Help" (see this file), and "Quit" (return to the system).  The "Input
File Format" and "Output File Format" menus allow you to select the Input
and Output file formats. (Input defaults to MaxiPlan "Save Data as Text"
format; Output has no default value, and MUST be entered before "Perform
Conversion" is enabled!)
    Once the output file format has been selected (BOTH selected input and
output formats are indicated with a check mark on the menu), you may
select "Perform Conversion."  You will then be asked to type in filenames,
which may include pathnames of any length, for both files; the program
will then process them, and return control to the menus.
    The option, "RRDS format" on the Input and Output file format menus
allows you to convert files to and from Relative Record format.  If it is 
selected, you will be prompted, after you enter the filenames, to enter
the record and field lengths for the file(s)

